    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] js_module.py _EXPORTABLE_KINDS unchanged @100b6fbb6e. Fixture fx_gafaj: `export const playlistStore = {byId(){}, all(){}}` + `export function helper()`; playlistStore is_exported=True but module_exports reaches only helper. Narrower consequence than the title says: a.ts's playlistStore.byId('x') still has a resolved calls edge to byId, and the file contains both playlistStore and its methods, so the module_exports traversal is what misses them, not every traversal. koel counts not re-measured. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFOUND 2026-10-01 by WI-sinol (branch jgstern-agent/fix/sinol), measured on koel.\n\nTHE GAP. module_exports is emitted only for kinds in js_module.py `_EXPORTABLE_KINDS` = {function, method, class, getter, setter, constructor}. An exported NON-callable binding -- `export const playlistStore = { ... }`, `export const http = new Http()`, `module.exports = sharp` where sharp is a variable -- is part of the module's public surface (the module_exports definition in edge_types.py: \"Module exposes a symbol as part of its public surface\") but never gets the edge.\n\nWHY IT SURFACED NOW. Before WI-sinol the linker sent module_exports to EVERY symbol of an exportable kind, so a koel store's object-literal methods (e.g. radioStationStore.ts `byId`) were reached file -> method directly, by accident. WI-sinol gates the edge on is_exported is True, which those methods are not (they are members of an exported object, not exports). A traversal a.ts -imports-> store.ts -module_exports-> ? now reaches neither the store nor its methods.\n\nNUMBERS (koel, WI-sinol branch survey): 111 JS/TS variables carry is_exported=True; 0 of them have a module_exports edge, before or after WI-sinol.\n\nDECISION NEEDED: add `variable` (and possibly `constant`) to the kinds the edge may reach, and whether an exported object literal should `contains` its methods so traversal continues. Not measured: the effect on slice / reverse-slice output.\nRelated: WI-sinol."  # c725
